      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mount Olive was officially incorporated on May 18, 1900, making it older than nearby towns Magee and Collins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Olive%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s railroad tracks were finished in 1899, and the railroad has been a lifeline for Mount Olive ever since.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofmtolivems.com/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in the valley of Okatoma Creek, Mount Olive sits within the Pascagoula River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Olive%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Town officials say Mount Olive’s core values are small‑town character, guided growth, and preserving its historical, cultural, and natural heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
